From 2077b8549b2396a2d2a0d2a5d52abfa057e826c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:23:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] android: Support autofocus without a lens control

The HAL enabled autofocus only for cameras with a LensFocusDistance
control. A sensor that focuses on its own (S5K4ECGX through the simple
pipeline) offers AfTrigger instead: treat that as autofocus support too,
with a minimum focus distance of 10 diopters (~10 cm, the sensor's macro
limit) and an uncalibrated focus distance.

The AfState of libcamera (Idle, Scanning, Focused, Failed) was passed on
unchanged as ANDROID_CONTROL_AF_STATE, whose values differ. Translate it:
in auto mode, and in a continuous mode after an AF trigger until the
next cancel, report ACTIVE_SCAN and FOCUSED_LOCKED / NOT_FOCUSED_LOCKED,
which apps wait for after a tap to focus or before a still; otherwise
the passive states.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Change-Id: I7772574cf147314c52f3a0614c59e6604d849c4b
---
 src/android/camera_capabilities.cpp | 12 +++++++++
 src/android/camera_device.cpp       | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
